  "description": "Architectural rules for .NET that break the build. Stricture.Net is a Roslyn analyzer toolkit that lets a project declare its architectural conventions — folder layout, type classification, file co-location, default visibility, and banned types/namespaces/packages — as assembly-level attributes, then surfaces violations as live IDE squiggles and dotnet build diagnostics. A single package reference delivers both the attribute library you reference and the analyzer that enforces it; consumers just write `using Stricture;`.",
  "id": "Stricture.Net",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-06-10T04:43:41.803Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "HyiPCwYGUmG4bRHhyrSzhs8taY78VtKo10HR0Jjxg1c4/Jm18bcz7e2OdyY4eU5CYe5Le1ZK73Ko5U8FMX6I1g==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 44897,
  "published": "2026-06-10T04:40:59.947Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.1 — Packaging and documentation. The package is now produced by a dedicated build project and ships the Abstractions XML documentation in lib/. No changes to attributes, rules, or diagnostics. Internal: source and tests reorganized to one type per file; version centralized in Directory.Build.props; README expanded and a CLAUDE.md added.\n\n1.0.0 — Initial release. Attribute-driven, per-assembly architectural rules (ARCH0001–ARCH4001): folder-structure layout (ARCH1001/1002), nested-type promotion (ARCH1003), interface-naming (ARCH1010), internal-by-default (ARCH1020), one-type-per-file and suffix co-location (ARCH2001/2002), and banned type/namespace/package usage (ARCH3001/4001), plus config validation (ARCH0001) and isolated rule-error reporting (ARCH0002). Ships the attribute library and the analyzer in a single package. All rules default to Warning; escalate to error per rule in .editorconfig.",
